{"id": "EUVD-2026-103817", "enisaUuid": "da177cb6-5c06-37f3-9529-cb399688a41b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: btintel: fix buffer over-read in btintel_hw_error()\n\nThe \"Exception info %s\" print uses skb->data + 1, but the 12-byte\npayload is not guaranteed to be NUL-terminated and can be read past\nits end.\n\nBound the print with \"%.*s\" and skb->len - 1.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:47:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/be58b239d2be5da7a7fac11d3eb8bf75dce6511b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bbc7de352f3f3864369c904aac944c7de84c6e7b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c42ce5373405ca93946311652c51ccfeb1c2d913", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/673f707518e8ef03306f84c512cb160971f175fe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/40eb4b18ad167b63644c27fa67a7400ba050379a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98732", "GHSA-ww29-ppp3-6wfc"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "147c4000-7c75-388e-b2a6-60d22410faf3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "973bb97e5aee56edddaae3d5c96877101ad509c0 <be58b239d2be5da7a7fac11d3eb8bf75dce6511b"}, {"id": "1fc4c974-8d8f-3c3f-94a6-020824cf2835", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "2094b405-6831-3ab6-930e-93827086e399", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "973bb97e5aee56edddaae3d5c96877101ad509c0 <40eb4b18ad167b63644c27fa67a7400ba050379a"}, {"id": "2b1b6da5-5a86-3ce3-9560-92683b92ea24", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "2b562968-9783-37da-8069-fe108d6ba9c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "4f6a5a82-02fa-3cc6-a53d-4b9238b8442f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_ve